{"subjectId":"cryptography","id":"ch9","title":"TLS / SSL","group":"Roadmap Chapters","order":18,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Transport Layer Security: comparing TLS 1.2 vs 1.3 handshakes, and step-by-step connection walkthroughs.</p>\n<section class=\"block\">\n<h3><i class=\"ti ti-shuffle\"></i>1. Comparison: TLS 1.2 vs. TLS 1.3</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Feature</th>\n<th>TLS 1.2 Handshake</th>\n<th>TLS 1.3 Handshake</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Round Trips (RTT)</strong></td>\n<td>2-RTT (requires 2 round trips before sending encrypted data).</td>\n<td>1-RTT (requires only 1 round trip, reducing latency).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Key Exchange</strong></td>\n<td>Supports RSA, Static DH, and Ephemeral DH.</td>\n<td>Mandates Ephemeral DH (ECDHE/DHE) to guarantee <strong>Forward Secrecy</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>0-RTT Mode</strong></td>\n<td>Not supported.</td>\n<td>Supported (allows returning clients to send encrypted data on the first request).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cipher Suites</strong></td>\n<td>Supports old, weak ciphers (RC4, 3DES, CBC mode).</td>\n<td>Only supports highly secure AEAD ciphers (AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"block\">\n<h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-left-right\"></i>2. TLS 1.3 Handshake Sequence</h3>\n<figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>Client                                                              Server\n  |                                                                   |\n  |---- ClientHello (Supported ciphers, DH key share A=g^a mod p) ---&gt;|\n  |                                                                   |\n  |                                 [Server selects cipher suite]     |\n  |                                 [Calculates Shared Secret]        |\n  |&lt;--- ServerHello (Selected cipher, DH key share B=g^b mod p) ------|\n  |&lt;--- Server Certificate &amp; Signature (Signed with CA Private Key) --|\n  |&lt;--- Finished (Encrypted validation tag) --------------------------|\n  |                                                                   |\n  | [Client verifies Server Certificate]                              |\n  | [Calculates Shared Secret]                                        |\n  |---- Finished (Encrypted validation tag) -------------------------&gt;|\n  |                                                                   |\n  |&lt;================== Encrypted Application Data ===================&gt;|</code></pre></figure>\n</section>"}